ed in the entity description and reinforced by its connection to the third-party transfer prohibition described in the relationships. [Data: Entities (583, +more); Relationships (589, +more)].\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"summary\": \"TERCEIRA PARTE is an external third party central to data-transfer constraints\",\n      \"explanation\": \"TERCEIRA PARTE is characterized as an external third party and recipient of data transfers within the data flow, making it a focal point for cross-organization data sharing decisions. This external role necessitates clear boundaries and oversight to prevent unauthorized data movements. [Data: Entities (591, +more); Relationships (589, +more)].\\n\\nThe document explicitly centers on prohibiting raw data transfers to third parties, positioning TERCEIRA PARTE as a critical constraint within the ecosystem. This prohibition drives compliance requirements, informs risk management, and shapes the operational tempo of data-sharing activities involving all parties. [Data: Relationships (589, +more); Entities (583, +more)].\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"summary\": \"Controlled data-sharing flow between INSTITUTO PESQUISA and TERCEIRA PARTE under anti-raw-data-transfer policy\",\n      \"explanation\": \"The INSTITUTO PESQUISA–TERCEIRA PARTE relationship reflects a controlled data-sharing dynamic where raw data transfers to third parties are prohibited, indicating a tightly regulated data exchange pipeline. This arrangement supports privacy protections while still enabling essential data collaboration under strict governance. [Data: Relationships (589, +more); Entities (583, +more)].\\n\\nThis constraint reduces the risk of data leakage and non-compliance, but it also imposes governance overhead to ensure that data sharing is mediated through approved processes, aggregates, or anonymized datasets as appropriate under Artigo 13 and ANPD guidelines. [Data: Relationships (589, +more); Entities (585, +more)].\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"summary\": \"Overall governance posture anchored by ANPD regulation and Artigo 13 controls\",\n      \"explanation\": \"The governance posture is anchored by ANPD regulation of health data research as described in Artigo 13, with an explicit framework for controlled access and privacy-preserving practices. This regulatory backbone is evidenced by the linkage between ARTIGO_13 and ANPD in the relationships set. [Data: Relationships (579, +more); Entities (585, +more)].\\n\\nCollectively, the combination of controlled access, illustrated authorization flow, and strict prohibition on raw data transfers to third parties points to a governance architecture designed to safeguard personal data while enabling ethically sound health research. [Data: Entities (585, +more); Relationships (581, +more); Relationships (589, +more)].\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"rating\": 6.0,\n  \"rating_explanation\": \"Regulatory governance and strict data-sharing controls create a moderate-to-high impact due to privacy, compliance, and data-flow constraints.\"\n}", "refusal": null, "role": "assistant", "annotations": null, "audio": null, "function_call": null, "tool_calls": null, "provider_specific_fields": {"reasoning": null, "refusal": null, "reasoning_details": [{"type": "reasoning.encrypted", "data": "gAAAAABqrv9RLt6FIWSHtZFzzT8ojorIi_t0tmvVgdFxkYPizYcRJb3eNXmasSM7J0dhTdCJIGvbmaBrj2uMlKIZR-ohJjM0wBTpqXc9dHiuQDHl-WBOBxB4Qp2YkQtl1AhiGP_jdNuElqPN4DaJqs0MpaCEFFukQh2ioTwH4r_hLZpQlzVCK5489NDoGDgDpB89Ib3EDqdSYakmO_LfwcsEHkbkvO5FK3gVXsFv4Llfyfpf2vCTaPQLT5W27vwi-4fgnleEMMwdipWX34tjvtWjMf8L06ojvNTWx6iMFgNcyHlFlZMF-4FIi6VI14HZTdyqZdmoRcb94tmVC8FQZcdrmgRXg-grSNJzMupb-r_FTPOD3n9XwTMUddaYmOrcfkOtI_r3J213MqzsEMGj0xfIq_OhgmLP9SEPz2282q-vrr6PRhk0Zut3vInUdF2_O1CX5YOkaqvkRR52R2I1aYoinqugCvdt4xrvxy2jxS0IPctP4hSakO3AQ5DLShhyD-9mYcnw7Ik8J_-eyWfroWCKg8dRNR1R-H06rf08lVkMVKLwtArwtXpf5XJKmqOLmLRtIOBg-0AzRO_dL9NZ2pXhZWg24DJvsNnPpbu7EHmZ7UOhNKZq_qP8pkIALZSsTB9pwRRxkutrMuAoqlB747Rqu1AFw_NvGiaVIkGzpH_qXA1CZwgsX-fik6so2ke4g3KxePojRCqMlIRybhXdX